blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.1.stable (14d19694e0c88a3f9e82d899a0400f27a24c176e)\n- Verified with Godot's own test runner (`--test gdscript-parser <file>`) built from a clean 4.6.1 checkout.\n- Not tested in earlier versions.\n\n### System information\n\nLinux 6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2 (x86_64) - Godot v4.6.1.stable - No rendering (headless)\n\n### Issue description\n\n`GDScriptParser::TreePrinter::print_match_pattern()` crashes with SIGSEGV (signal 11) when printing the AST of a valid GDScript file containing dictionary match patterns. The parser accepts the file without errors, but the debug TreePrinter dereferences a null `PatternNode*` pointer during recursive pattern printing.\n\nThe crash occurs specifically in `print_match_pattern()` calling itself recursively for a nested dictionary pattern - frame # 0 and # 1 in the backtrace are both `print_match_pattern()`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Save the following as `crash.gd`:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc f(x):\n\tmatch x:\n\t\t{\"a\"}:\n\t\t\tpass\n```\n\n2. Run Godot's built-in GDScript parser test:\n   ```\n   godot --headless --test gdscript-parser crash.gd\n   ```\n\n3. Observe SIGSEGV (signal 11) in `print_match_pattern()`.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSingle 4-line file `crash.gd` above. Any dictionary match pattern with a key-only entry (no `: value`) triggers the crash. Empty `{}` does not crash (loop body never executes). Reproducible via Godot's own `--test gdscript-parser` command on a clean 4.6.1 build with `tests=yes`.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{